WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:06.180
The townsfolk scream and run in terror, their
flaming torches and pitchforks falling from

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.420
their trembling hands.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.390
Behind them, SCP-096 roars in monstrous rage.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:15.170
It will kill every single one of them.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:20.529
And to think, this had been the happiest few
weeks of its life not long before…

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:26.630
SCP-096 is one of the most fearsome anomalies
ever contained by the SCP Foundation.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:32.509
Responsible for nearly as many containment
breaches and personnel casualties as SCP-682,

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:38.670
the Shy Guy is known for only a few things:
its long, pale limbs, its tendency to huddle

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:43.930
in the corner of its cell, weeping, and the
fact that anyone who sees its face is doomed

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.420
to meet a horrible, violent fate.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:52.859
Most of the researchers and civilians alike
who have crossed SCP-096's past would have

00:00:52.859 --> 00:00:58.539
no trouble describing it as a monster, and
some might even use stronger language than

00:00:58.539 --> 00:00:59.539
that.

00:00:59.539 --> 00:01:05.720
But, though SCP-096 is certainly frightening
to behold, and often deadly to those who behold

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:10.900
all of it, the Shy Guy is not a monster, not
to everyone.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:14.280
Once upon a time, it even had a friend.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:21.360
Many, many years ago, before the SCP Foundation
first contained SCP-096, it was just a pale

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:27.150
figure that hid from sight in the dense, snowy
forest on a remote mountainside.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:33.079
There, its long, lanky body and unnaturally
pale complexion allowed the creature to blend

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:39.049
in with the landscape, skin like snow and
arms and legs like branches and slender tree

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:40.049
trunks.

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:45.299
No one ever came into its domain, save for
the occasional lost hiker, and it was easy

00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:48.990
enough for the Shy Guy to duck out of sight
when they did come.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:53.200
In the warmer months, crews of lumberjacks
would come through, and the Shy Guy would

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.719
have to be more careful with its hiding, moving
quickly to keep its face obscured from the

00:01:58.719 --> 00:01:59.719
strangers.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:03.689
None of them ever saw its face, though they
could feel its presence.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:08.520
They would whisper amongst themselves about
the feeling of being watched, recalling old

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:13.800
lumberjack legends of "the hidebehind," a
creature that stalked through forests and

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.970
hid itself behind the trees whenever its prey
turned to look.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:23.750
The Shy Guy wasn't trying to hunt them, it
only wanted to be left alone, but the lumberjacks

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:28.770
still glanced over their shoulders nervously
as they went about their work, swapping scary

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:32.720
stories around the campfire at night when
the work was done.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.470
But other than a rustling branch, a flash
of white darting between the trees, or the

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:42.630
occasional set of unnaturally large footprints
in the snow, they never saw the creature they

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.550
could sense sharing the woods with them.

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:50.270
It was for the best that they didn't, they
wouldn't have survived if they had managed

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.830
to catch a glimpse of its face.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:57.800
The Shy Guy was happy with its home, or at
least as happy as it could be about anything

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:58.960
in its life.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.080
It was a lonely existence, never letting anyone
truly see it.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:08.700
The creature's life was ruled by fear and
isolation, the terror that one day its face

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.650
would be spotted and it would be unable to
control what it did next.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:18.200
Late at night, when the world was asleep save
for a few owls nestled in the branches up

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:23.640
above and scanning the ground for mice to
eat, the Shy Guy would let itself truly feel

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:29.280
the weight of its suffering, crying so hard
its sobs shook the treeline.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:34.420
But other times, when the land was still and
quiet, when a fresh snowfall blanketed the

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:40.959
earth in soft, white powder and all living
things were hiding in a warm place until springtime

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:45.720
came, SCP-096 felt something like peace.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:50.970
The dead of Winter was its safest time, a
time when it wouldn't need to listen for every

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.560
sound and await potential intruders.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:56.890
But, of course, Winter never lasted.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:58.940
Eventually, Spring would always come.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:04.000
The first blades of green grass would poke
up through the melting snow, and life would

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.849
return to the Shy Guy's forest.

00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:10.890
One day, the Shy Guy's guard dropped, and
it made a grave mistake.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.510
It allowed someone to get too close before
looking for a hiding spot.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:19.720
A man, from one of the lumber camps setting
up nearby, saw the creature's face.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:24.660
The man screamed in shock and terror, but
his screams were soon drowned out by the raw,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:30.590
animalistic bellow of the Shy Guy as it flew
into an uncontrollable frenzy of rage and

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:34.440
despair, chasing the man through the forest
at breakneck speed.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:39.660
It was far faster than the man, running on
longer, stronger legs than any human could

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:40.660
have.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:44.500
When it caught up to the man, in a foreign
part of the forest that the creature had not

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:48.440
seen before, it silenced his screams for good.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.340
All at once, the creature was alone once more.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:58.090
Then came the remorse, the inevitable feeling
of deep, devastating loss that came over it

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:02.400
every time it destroyed a person who had seen
its face.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:08.080
The same cycle, over and over again, relentless
and unceasing.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:12.520
Though it should have gotten used to the whole
thing by now, it broke the poor creature's

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.520
heart.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:19.470
Succumbing to the sadness, SCP-096 slumped
to the ground, cradling its head in its massive

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.080
hands, and began to cry.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.590
"Are you alright, there?

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.730
Are you hurt?"

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:26.800
A voice suddenly interrupted the creature's
private lament.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:31.669
It froze at the sound, before lifting its
head to seek out the source of the interruption.

00:05:31.669 --> 00:05:33.120
Who was that?

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.120
Where were they?

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:37.190
Did it have time to hide before they could
see its face?

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:42.120
The Shy Guy opened its eyes to see an old
man standing only a few feet away from it,

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.490
holding a cane.

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:48.940
The man was facing it, his eyes aimed toward
the Shy Guy's face, but they were unfocused.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.180
They could not see.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:55.001
The Shy Guy didn't entirely understand how,
but it knew that the man was unable to see

00:05:55.001 --> 00:05:56.220
its face.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:06:01.560
For the first time in a very long time, it
felt relief wash over it.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.080
"You stopped crying.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.610
Can you speak?"

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:08.550
The man walked closer to the creature, concern
furrowing his brow.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:12.340
"Here, take my hand and come inside where
it's warm.

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.220
I'll get you a blanket and something to eat."

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:21.530
The old man held out his hand expectantly,
and slowly, hesitantly, SCP-096 placed its

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.530
hand in his.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:25.750
"My, you're a big fellow!

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:28.130
If you can stand, come with me.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.750
We'll get you all sorted out."

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:35.849
Unsure, but too surprised to do anything else,
the Shy Guy silently followed the old blind

00:06:35.849 --> 00:06:38.150
man into a nearby cabin.

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:44.389
Inside, it was indeed warm, the small yet
pleasant space lit by a crackling fire in

00:06:44.389 --> 00:06:45.389
the hearth.

00:06:45.389 --> 00:06:53.289
It was the nicest place SCP-096 had ever been,
cozy and dry, no snow or mud to be found.

00:06:53.289 --> 00:06:58.030
Every surface was smooth or soft, made for
living comfortably.

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:03.009
The old man led the creature to a little dining
table, and pulled out a chair, inviting it

00:07:03.009 --> 00:07:04.040
to sit down.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:09.699
He prattled on about how nice it was to have
some company for once, even if his new companion

00:07:09.699 --> 00:07:11.169
was unable to speak.

00:07:11.169 --> 00:07:15.729
He had plenty to say, and was happy to fill
the silence enough for the both of them.

00:07:15.729 --> 00:07:21.590
He turned on a radio, and it came to life
with the sound of music and crackling static,

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:26.090
then he busied himself at the wood fire stove
where a pot of soup was simmering.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:31.830
He poured two bowls of soup, one for him,
and one for the Shy Guy, and placed them both

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.860
on the table.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:39.400
SCP-096 wasn't sure what to make of the cabin,
the soup, or the spoon that the old man handed

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:40.650
it to go with the meal.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:45.360
After a moment of watching the old man eat,
however, it began to understand that this

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.430
was food.

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:51.180
It disregarded the spoon in favor of picking
up the bowl, drinking straight from it.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:56.831
The broth, meat, and vegetables warmed the
creature from the inside out in a way it had

00:07:56.831 --> 00:08:03.900
never felt before, and for once the Shy Guy
made a sound other than a screech or a sob.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:04.900
"Mm!"

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:09.710
The old man laughed delightedly, and agreed
that the soup was indeed very good.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:13.900
The two ate the rest of their meal, and the
old man placed a heavy blanket on the couch

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:17.060
for the creature, inviting it to stay the
night.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:20.039
In fact, it could stay as long as it wanted.

00:08:20.039 --> 00:08:24.520
Like he had said, the old man could really
use the company, as well as an extra pair

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.909
of hands to help out around the house.

00:08:26.909 --> 00:08:30.490
This could, he said, be an arrangement that
benefitted them both!

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:34.850
With that, the old man went to bed, leaving
the Shy Guy alone for the night.

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:40.510
It considered leaving while the man slept,
slinking back off into the forest and disappearing,

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:45.680
but as it pulled the blanket over its body,
it felt a sense of warmth and comfort enveloping

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:46.680
it.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:52.970
This was a safe place, one where no one would
catch it unawares and look at its face.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:56.089
Maybe it could stay, at least for a little
while.

00:08:56.089 --> 00:09:01.269
Before long, the Shy Guy's eyes closed, and
it drifted off to sleep.

00:09:01.269 --> 00:09:05.550
The Shy Guy and the old man quickly fell into
a routine from there.

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:09.970
The old man taught the creature how to tidy
up around the cabin, how to chop wood and

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:12.520
use it to keep the stove and fireplace lit.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:17.750
He showed it how to open cans of beans and
retrieve meat from the cabin's smokehouse

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:22.640
so they could fix their meals, and introduced
the creature to all of his favorite stations

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.160
on the radio.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:28.930
All the while, the old man talked, telling
the creature stories of his life: his time

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:34.310
in the army, how he met his wife, how it felt
to lose her, how difficult it was to raise

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:39.630
his children alone, and how rewarding it was
to see them go off and start families of their

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:40.630
own.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:45.570
During one of these stories, the old man remarked
that his family would be coming out to visit

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:49.589
soon, and bring him some supplies to help
him through the rest of winter before the

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:51.269
warm weather returned.

00:09:51.269 --> 00:09:55.470
The Shy Guy should have understood what that
meant, should have planned to leave before

00:09:55.470 --> 00:10:00.980
the man's family arrived, but it was so overwhelmed
by the joys of its new life that it didn't

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:02.770
even consider the possibility.

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:07.860
In this moment, it seemed that things would
always be perfect.

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:11.110
One morning, the Shy Guy awoke to the sound
of a knock at the door.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:14.410
It jolted awake at the sound, gasping with
fear.

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:17.480
The Old Man rushed into the room, grinning
excitedly.

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:22.370
He told the Shy Guy not to be afraid, that
this was only his son coming to visit.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:24.240
But SCP-096 panicked.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:26.020
It had to cover its face!

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.020
Now!

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:31.360
As the old man opened the door to welcome
his son inside, the Shy Guy quickly buried

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:34.899
its face in its hands, shielding it from the
young man's eyes.

00:10:34.899 --> 00:10:39.389
Though the young man did not doom himself
by seeing the creature's face, he couldn't

00:10:39.389 --> 00:10:43.300
help but cry out in shock at the sight of
his father's houseguest.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:48.130
He tried to explain to his father that this
was not an ordinary man in need of shelter,

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.560
but rather some sort of terrible monster.

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:55.959
He described the Shy Guy to his father, its
lack of clothing, its emaciated form, and

00:10:55.959 --> 00:11:00.120
impossible height, but the old man would not
listen to a word.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:04.420
He shooed his son out of the cabin, insisting
that if he was going to be rude to his guest,

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:06.959
then he could go ahead and see himself out.

00:11:06.959 --> 00:11:11.250
He told his son that the Shy Guy, no matter
how strange it might look, had been a great

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:16.730
help and comfort to him, and he would not
tolerate a rude word against his new friend.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:22.830
He slammed the door shut, then apologized
to SCP-096 for his son's behavior.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:25.240
Meanwhile, his son was distraught.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:28.100
His poor father, living alone with a monster!

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:31.270
He could not sit idly by while this continued.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:35.330
He rushed into town, and told everyone all
about what he had seen.

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:39.720
Local lumberjacks spoke up with their own
stories, telling him about the legends of

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:44.279
the Hidebehind, and the lumberjack who had
gone out on a job in those woods and never

00:11:44.279 --> 00:11:46.260
returned home.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:51.860
This creature living with the old man had
to be the same monster!

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:57.300
The townspeople decided that enough was enough,
and they were going to take back the forest,

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:00.610
and handle this monster problem once and for
all.

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:04.910
They grabbed whatever weapons they could find,
from hunting rifles and kitchen knives to

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.810
pitchforks and torches.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:12.010
All the while, they worked themselves up into
a frenzy of fear and anger.

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:16.649
Before long, the once-peaceful people of the
town had formed into an angry mob, with the

00:12:16.649 --> 00:12:19.670
old man's son at the helm.

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:20.670
"Kill the Monster!"

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:25.190
They cheered, as they stormed into the forest
and toward the old man's cabin.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:29.949
The old man opened his door, expecting to
find his son standing there again, and was

00:12:29.949 --> 00:12:35.320
greeted instead by everyone from his town,
armed to the teeth and ready for a fight.

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:38.440
They demanded to see the Monster that he was
keeping inside.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:43.360
When he refused, a group of men grabbed him
by the arms, dragging him out of the cabin.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:48.070
As he protested, they insisted that they were
doing this for his own good, to protect him

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:52.180
from the hideous beast he had unknowingly
welcomed into his home.

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:56.570
He struggled to break free, but he was not
as strong as he had been in his youth, and

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:58.390
he was outnumbered.

00:12:58.390 --> 00:13:04.070
SCP-096 watched as its friend was pulled from
the cabin and taken outside, and it was unable

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:05.700
to stop itself from intervening.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:09.510
It ran out of the front door, where the angry
mob was waiting.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:15.339
Neither SCP-096 nor the mob were prepared
for what happened next, when the dozens of

00:13:15.339 --> 00:13:21.029
people standing there with their pitchforks
and torches all found their eyes locked directly

00:13:21.029 --> 00:13:24.220
onto SCP-096's face.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:29.959
The creature had been upset before, but now
it was positively furious.

00:13:29.959 --> 00:13:34.630
Its mouth stretched into a shriek that echoed
off the mountainside, and it began to rip

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:39.500
through the crowd like tissue paper, massive
arms swinging and knocking over people left

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.920
and right until no one was left standing.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:47.010
Some of the townspeople tried to fight back,
to prod at the creature with their pitchforks

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:51.881
or swipe at it with the flames of their torches,
but the attacks didn't even slow the Shy Guy

00:13:51.881 --> 00:13:52.881
down.

00:13:52.881 --> 00:13:57.420
Bullets fired from the feet of hunting rifles
ricocheted off of the creature's skin, not

00:13:57.420 --> 00:14:00.769
leaving so much as a dent as it tore the crowd
apart.

00:14:00.769 --> 00:14:06.240
By the time it was through, there was no one
left except for the old man and his son.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:11.100
The old man called out to the creature, asking
what had happened, asking if it was alright.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:14.300
But, as always, the creature could not answer.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:18.259
And even if it could, it wouldn't have said
a word at that moment.

00:14:18.259 --> 00:14:23.800
Its focus was elsewhere, its eyes trained
on the old man's son, the only person who

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:26.510
had seen its face and was still alive.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:31.560
The young man ran off into the forest as fast
as he could, tripping over his own feet as

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:34.750
the terror made him too clumsy to see straight.

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:39.560
The attempt to escape was in vain, and the
Shy Guy took no time at all to catch up with

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:40.560
him.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:45.230
It grabbed the young man in its hands, lifted
him into the air as he squirmed and fought

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.480
to break free.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:50.649
Then, it unhinged its jaw, and swallowed him
whole.

00:14:50.649 --> 00:14:56.079
When the Shy Guy quieted, all of its prey
disposed of, it heard the voice of the old

00:14:56.079 --> 00:14:58.600
man in the distance, calling out for his friend.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:03.880
It knew, then, that it could never go back
to the only person who had ever shown it kindness.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:06.920
It would not be safe, for either of them.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:11.990
Instead, it would return to the deep, deep
forest, to the life of solitude.

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:18.660
But it would never forget that time in the
cabin, or the only man who ever made SCP-096

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:21.320
feel as if it wasn't a monster at all.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:27.859
Now go check out “SCP-096 VS Siren Head”
and “SCP-096’s Sad END!” for more!

